            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of acute myocardial infarction with the x-sizer coronary thrombectomy device].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>793-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The abundant thrombi present in infarct-related arteries may impair the angiographic result of primary angioplasty in acute myocardial infarction. We describe the utilization of the thrombus-removal device X-Sizer before coronary stenting in 4 patients with acute myocardial infarction treated with primary angioplasty. The procedure was successful in all the cases and the patients were discharged without complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
